@SamFerracin 
> what is the behaviour in the legacy sampler/estimator?

Legacy estimator warns as well, but it does so only for options which were explicitly set by the user. As I said, once we switch to pydantic models, we can be more selective and only warn when something was explicitly set.

@SamFerracin @diego-plan9 
I think this issue could be closed as completed?
There is one stretch goal which hasn't been completed, but its merit could be debated, and even if we choose to pursue it, I don't think it should block the epic.

@SamFerracin 
> and see if we get a bool?

Yes, it goes through end to end.
